# fixedbugs, defect 2555, lane b38-module, 2026-11-15.
#
# A fetched package's header embedding its own data file, `#embed
# "data.bin"`. clang's `-M` writes an `#embed` target whole beside the
# package's root written relative, and C2 compared the two spellings, so the
# header was refused `package_reads_outside`, a false message: the file lies
# inside the root. The refusal stands for its true reason, told now: `#embed`
# is C23's, and every warning clang gives in a header's own code but
# `-Wall`'s is an error (panel 245's R1). Needs clang 19 or later, which
# knows `#embed`; at the floor, clang 18, the line is no directive at all.
use <pk>/pk

function main()
    print(pk.first())
